# --- Weekly bounty (docs/bounty.md) ----------------------------------------
# The prize goes to the fastest win of the week's CITY GP, read off the board.
# Prize weeks are posted in the Convex dashboard (bountyWeeks table): set the
# production deployment URL once and no bounty ever needs a redeploy. Public.
# The same URL carries the worldwide boards — today's daily, the fastest bounty
# wins and the Weekend GP ghosts (convex/boards.ts, convex/weekend.ts). Without
# it every board falls back to the one held on the phone.
#VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://your-deployment.convex.cloud
# Without Convex: the ISO week a prize is posted (the bounty card lights up and
# only that week) and its prize text, at build time.
# Both are ignored once VITE_CONVEX_URL is set.
#VITE_BOUNTY_WEEK=2026-W38
#VITE_BOUNTY_PRIZE=5,000 COINS

# Sign-in before buying is off by default: the garage key on the player's device
# is their access. To require a login, set this AND SHOP_SIGN_IN=required in Convex.
#VITE_SHOP_SIGN_IN=required

# Optional override for the NEAR Auth testnet preview. The shared development
# client is used by default. Register callback URLs/origins with your auth provider.
# This is a public client ID, never put a client secret in VITE_ variables.
#VITE_NEAR_AUTH_CLIENT_ID=your-testnet-client-id
# The shared client accepts http://localhost:3000 for local login.
# Run npm run dev:auth; use localhost exactly, not 127.0.0.1.
# If overridden, set the same public ID as NEAR_AUTH_CLIENT_ID in Convex.
# Deploy convex/auth.config.ts and the relay handlers for server-side purchase gates.

# Ownership verification uses backend-only Convex settings, not VITE_ variables:
# NEAR_AUTH_PROOFS_ENABLED, NEAR_AUTH_SIGN_DEPOSIT_YOCTO,
# NEAR_AUTH_ALLOWED_ORIGINS. Disabled by default; see docs/near-economy.md
# for the testnet setup, sponsorship limits and remaining live verification.

# Limited editions (cars sold for NEAR). Backend-only Convex settings for the
# testnet "Get test NEAR" button; it never runs on mainnet.
# NEAR_TEST_GRANT=2            test NEAR per garage, once
# NEAR_TEST_GRANT_DAILY=20     garages topped up per UTC day
# NEAR_TEST_GRANT_RESERVE=3    NEAR the game account always keeps back
# NEAR_DEALER_AGENTS_ENABLED=false  disable automatic dealers on dev when prod
# uses the same on-chain dealer accounts; leave enabled on only one deployment.
